Morphysm — licensing

From the Morphysm corpus.

Two licences apply, depending on the material. Both forbid derivatives: no altered
version of any Morphysm text may be distributed. They differ only on commercial use.


THE THREE RELEASED VOLUMES — CC BY-NC-ND 4.0
  The Infernal Codex of Cain: Secrets of the Morning Star
  The Black Book of Morphysm (Extended, AI Integration)
  The Burning Book of Morphysm 2 (AI)
  and the released PDF editions of each.

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/


EVERYTHING ELSE — CC BY-ND 4.0
  The pamphlet in all four languages, and every text under corpus/.

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/


You are free to:
  Share — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format, unchanged.
          For the three volumes, for non-commercial purposes only.

Under the following terms:
  Attribution   — You must give appropriate credit and provide a link to the licence.
  NoDerivatives — If you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you may not
                  distribute the modified material.
  NonCommercial — Applies to the three released volumes only: you may not use them
                  for commercial purposes.

The doctrine may be quoted, discussed, criticised and taught. It may not be edited
and re-issued as Morphysm. Ideas are not owned; this text is.

Per-text terms are recorded in corpus/manifest.json under "license", together with
the sha256 of every file as served. An altered copy is provably not the original:
verify against corpus/SHA256SUMS.

Published under the pen name J.K. — XXVI. The doctrine recognizes no personal
authorship.

Note on earlier copies: the pamphlet was published under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 before this
change. A Creative Commons licence, once granted, cannot be revoked. Copies obtained
under those terms keep the rights granted then.
